\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Is there one absolute $\sigma >0$ and a randomized polynomial-bit-time algorithm for arbitrary finite rational metric k-median that opens at most k facilities and achieves ratio $2-\sigma $ in expectation and with failure probability at most $(|clients|+|facilities|+2)^{-a}$ for any prescribed fixed $a>0$?

\subsection{Short English statement}
Is there one absolute $\sigma >0$ and a randomized polynomial-bit-time algorithm for arbitrary finite rational metric k-median that opens at most k facilities and achieves ratio $2-\sigma $ in expectation and with failure probability at most $(|clients|+|facilities|+2)^{-a}$ for any prescribed fixed $a>0$?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Single-Exponential-Recovery-and-Bounded-Price-Strictness-for-Metric-k-Median-September-24-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

