\section*{Metric k-median strictly below factor two}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents the following claims relevant to this question, with manuscript numbers following paper order in Sources. In manuscript 1 (family 125; 2026-09-24), the asserted result is that metric $k$-median admits exact-budget recovery from nearly complete proxy anchors, and a compatible bounded-price argument yields an absolute factor below two on arbitrary rational metrics.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
For manuscript 1 (family 125; 2026-09-24), sampled balls are completed using a partition-constrained submodular maximization that separates destinations without sampled proxies. A stability dichotomy combines recovery with one certified surplus execution, paying for removals while opening no more than the original facility budget.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The result supplies the conclusion in this problem with its displayed hypotheses and quantifiers. The broader statements and applications in the manuscript are kept separate from the particular question above. The supporting result is manuscript 1 (family 125; 2026-09-24).

\subsection{Formal verification}
For manuscript 1 (family 125; 2026-09-24), OpenAI lists Lean statements for this assertion: metric $k$-median admits exact-budget recovery from nearly complete proxy anchors, and a compatible bounded-price argument yields an absolute factor below two on arbitrary rational metrics.

The selected statement includes the clause used for this problem.

The linked family Comparator checks are \texttt{KMedianRecovery.lean}, \texttt{KMedianRefinedRecovery.lean}, \texttt{KMedianThreshold.lean}, \texttt{MetricKMedian.lean}.

Their named declarations include \texttt{OAI.MetricKMedian.main\_finite\_work}, \texttt{OAI.MetricKMedian.threshold}, \texttt{OAI.MetricKMedianRecovery.RefinedRecovery.refined\_recovery}, \texttt{OAI.MetricKMedianRecovery.global\_application}.

This site has not executed the Lean code. Described statement coverage is not an independent proof check.

\subsection{Status caveat}
The manuscripts were produced by an internal OpenAI model. OpenAI cautions that results without formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently checked the proofs; the label records the scope of OpenAI's claim.

